```

Not re-exported at the crate root; use `michi_core::redact::…`.

- `redact_secrets` replaces each known secret with `[REDACTED]`. Empty secrets are ignored, the longest secret wins when one contains another, and the text is scanned once, so the marker is never searched again and redacting twice changes nothing (unless a secret can match part of the marker, such as `RED` or `[`).
- `redact_url_userinfo` replaces the `user:password@` part of every `scheme://…` URL. A URL ends at whitespace, a quote, a backtick, `<` or `>`; everything up to the last `@` inside it is userinfo, so a password containing `@` or `/` is removed whole. A URL with no userinfo but an `@` later in its path (`https://host/pkg@1.2`) is over-redacted; that is the safe direction. Email addresses are not URLs and pass through. Also matched: the JSON-escaped separator `:\/\/`, the percent-encoded separator `%3A%2F%2F` (userinfo ends at the last `@` or `%40`), and a `"` or `'` inside the password (the text after the quote is searched for an `@` until a `/`, `\`, `?` or `#`; `"https://host","k":"a@b"` is over-redacted).
- `redact_common_shapes` is `redact_url_userinfo` plus the value of any `key=value` pair whose key names a secret, plus well-known token shapes. Keys: `key`, `sig`, `auth`, `pwd`, anything ending `_key`, `_sig` or `_auth`, starting `auth_`, or containing `token`, `secret`, `passw`, `signature`, `apikey`, `api_key`, `credential` or `authoriz` (case-insensitive, `-` read as `_`). The value runs to whitespace, `&`, a quote, a backtick, `)`, `<` or `>`. Token shapes: `ghp_`, `gho_`, `ghu_`, `ghs_`, `ghr_`, `github_pat_`, `npm_` and `pypi-` followed by 16 or more token characters, and `Bearer ` followed by 16 or more. It repeats until the text stops changing, so redacting twice equals redacting once. A fuzz target (`fuzz/fuzz_targets/redact.rs`) checks that and that a planted secret does not survive in any covered shape.
- **Not covered.** A JSON field (`"password": "x"`), a connection string without `://`, a secret in a URL path segment, a key or token with another prefix, an encoded or split value, and a value under a key the list above does not name. These helpers are a second line of defense after keeping secrets out of messages; "redacted" means "known shapes removed", not "safe to show".
- `DomainError::from_error` and `from_error_with_causes` apply `redact_common_shapes` to the error text they copy, because URLs with credentials and tokens in the query are the common leak in errors from HTTP and database clients (`reqwest` puts the whole URL in its top-level `Display`). The pipeline's `From<ExecutionError> for DomainError` does the same to step text (see `08-pipeline-execution.md`). `DomainError::new`, `cause` and `hint` take tool-author text and do not redact it.

