p='crates/michi-core/src/redact.rs'
s=open(p).read()
s=s.replace('''//!   \`key=value\` pairs whose key names a secret (\`token\`, \`api_key\`, \`password\`, ...), and a few well-known token
//!   shapes (\`ghp_\`, \`github_pat_\`, \`npm_\`, \`pypi-\`, \`Bearer\`).''','''//!   \`key=value\` pairs and \`Key: value\` headers whose key names a secret (\`token\`, \`api_key\`, \`password\`,
//!   \`Authorization\`, \`Cookie\`, ...), quoted or not, and a few well-known token shapes (\`ghp_\`, \`github_pat_\`,
//!   \`npm_\`, \`pypi-\`, \`Bearer\`).''')
a=s.index('//! **What this does not cover.**')
b=s.index('/// What a redacted value')
s=s[:a]+'''//! **What this does not cover.** A secret that is not a known value, not in a URL, not in a pair or header with a
//! telling key and not one of the listed token shapes passes through. Known gaps: a secret with a space in it
//! (`token=a b` loses only `a`), a value on the line after its key (YAML `password:` then an indented value), a command
//! line flag (`--password hunter2`), an encoded separator (`token%3Dvalue`), a key spelled with lookalike letters or
//! zero-width characters, a bare JWT, cloud key (`AKIA...`) or PEM private key block, a connection string without
//! `://`, a session id under a key that does not say so, and an encoded or split value. These helpers are a second line
//! of defense after keeping secrets out of messages in the first place. \"Redacted\" here means \"we looked for these
//! shapes\", never \"safe to show\".

'''+s[b:]
s=s.replace('''/// - A value after \`key=\` (query string, form body, log line) when the key, lowercased with \`-\` read as \`_\`, is \`key\`,
///   \`sig\`, \`auth\`, \`pwd\`, ends in \`_key\`, \`_sig\` or \`_auth\`, starts with \`auth_\`, or contains \`token\`, \`secret\`,
///   \`passw\`, \`signature\`, \`apikey\`, \`api_key\`, \`credential\` or \`authoriz\`. The value runs to whitespace, \`&\`, a
///   quote, a backtick, \`)\`, \`<\` or \`>\`. Other keys (\`page\`, \`status_code\`, \`monkey\`) are kept.''','''/// - A value after \`key=\` or \`key:\` (query string, form body, log line, HTTP header, JSON or Python-repr field, also
///   with the fullwidth \`＝\` and \`：\`, blanks around the separator and a quoted or JSON-escaped key) when the key,
///   lowercased with \`-\` read as \`_\`, is \`key\`, \`sig\`, \`auth\`, \`pwd\`, ends in \`_key\`, \`_sig\` or \`_auth\`, starts with
///   \`auth_\`, or contains \`token\`, \`secret\`, \`passw\`, \`signature\`, \`apikey\`, \`api_key\`, \`credential\`, \`authoriz\` or
///   \`cookie\`. Other keys (\`page\`, \`status_code\`, \`monkey\`) are kept.
/// - How far the value runs: a quoted value (\`\"\`, \`'\` or the JSON-escaped \`\\\\\"\`) to its closing quote, honoring \`\\\\\`
///   escapes and ending at a newline if unclosed; the quotes stay. After a scheme word (\`Basic\`, \`Bearer\`, \`Token\`,
///   \`Negotiate\`, \`NTLM\`, \`Bot\`, \`Digest\`, either case) the credential is redacted and the word kept
///   (\`Authorization: Basic [REDACTED]\`); \`Digest\` takes the rest of the line. A cookie key takes the rest of the line.
///   Otherwise the value runs to whitespace, \`&\`, a quote, a backtick, \`)\`, \`<\` or \`>\`. \`scheme://\` after a \`:\` is a
///   URL, not a value.''')
open(p,'w').write(s)
"
